<title>EGYPT: Egypt Eastern div 4.00 pounds/share.</title>
<headline>Egypt Eastern div 4.00 pounds/share.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt's sole cigarette manufacturer Eastern Company is to pay a dividend of four pounds a share for the 1995/96 financial year, a statement published in Al-Akhbar newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>The dividend is payable at Bank of Alexandria from January 5.</p>
<p>The dividend was four pounds in 1994/95. The year ends on June 30.</p>
<p>Brokers said the company's after-tax profit was 142.7 million pounds ($41.9 million) in 1995/96, up from 139.7 million in 1994/95.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom 20 2 578-3290/1</p>
